  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html",
    "href": "contributing/index.html",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Anyone in the lab can edit this site. Small fixes can be made in the browser on GitHub. Bigger changes are easier on your own computer.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#quick-fix-in-the-browser",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#quick-fix-in-the-browser",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Quick fix in the browser",
    "text": "Quick fix in the browser\nClick Edit this page (under the table of contents on the right) on any page. GitHub opens the source file. Make the change and open a pull request. The site rebuilds after the pull request is merged into main.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#working-on-your-own-computer",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#working-on-your-own-computer",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Working on your own computer",
    "text": "Working on your own computer\n\nInstall Quarto. RStudio and Positron already include it.\nClone this repository.\nFrom the repository folder, run:\n\nquarto preview\nThe site opens in your browser and reloads every time you save a file.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#adding-a-page",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#adding-a-page",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Adding a page",
    "text": "Adding a page\n\nCopy _templates/page.qmd into the folder for the section it belongs in, for example protocols/fruit-firmness.qmd. Use lowercase file names with hyphens.\nFill in title, description, and order at the top of the file.\nSave. The page appears in the sidebar on its own. You do not need to edit _quarto.yml.\n\nTo add a whole new section, make a new folder containing an index.qmd. That page’s title becomes the sidebar heading, and its order sets where the section appears.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#images",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#images",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Images",
    "text": "Images\nPut images in an images/ folder inside the section and always write alt text. See Quarto syntax for the format.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#pages-that-run-code",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#pages-that-run-code",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Pages that run code",
    "text": "Pages that run code\nIf a page runs R or Python code, render it on your computer before pushing (quarto render path/to/page.qmd) and commit the _freeze/ folder along with your page. The GitHub build reuses those stored results and never runs your code, so it does not need R, Python, or your packages.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#submitting-changes",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#submitting-changes",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Submitting changes",
    "text": "Submitting changes\ngit switch -c fix-nextcloud-page     # new branch\n# ...edit, preview, save...\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Update Nextcloud folder structure\"\ngit push -u origin fix-nextcloud-page\nThen open a pull request on GitHub. Once it is merged into main, the site publishes in a few minutes.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/index.html#writing-guidelines",
    "href": "contributing/index.html#writing-guidelines",
    "title": "Contributing",
    "section": "Writing guidelines",
    "text": "Writing guidelines\n\nOne topic per page.\nWrite steps that someone new can follow without asking you.\nLink to the source of truth (Breedbase, a pipeline’s own repository) instead of copying details that change.\nIf a step has a common failure, add a Troubleshooting section rather than burying it in the steps.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Everything here is regular Markdown plus a few Quarto additions. Each example shows the source, then what it looks like.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#callouts",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#callouts",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Callouts",
    "text": "Callouts\nFive types: note, tip, warning, important, caution.\n::: {.callout-tip}\n## Label tubes before grinding\nMarker rubs off once tubes are frozen.\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTipLabel tubes before grinding\n\n\n\nMarker rubs off once tubes are frozen.\n\n\nAdd collapse=\"true\" to make one that starts folded:\n::: {.callout-note collapse=\"true\"}\n## Why we do it this way\nBackground that most readers can skip.\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNoteWhy we do it this way\n\n\n\n\n\nBackground that most readers can skip.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#tabs",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#tabs",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Tabs",
    "text": "Tabs\nGood for instructions that differ by operating system or by crop.\n::: {.panel-tabset}\n## Windows\nUse WinSCP.\n\n## macOS / Linux\nUse rclone.\n:::\n\nWindowsmacOS / Linux\n\n\nUse WinSCP.\n\n\nUse rclone.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#code-blocks",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#code-blocks",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Code blocks",
    "text": "Code blocks\nName the language for syntax highlighting. Add a filename when it helps.\n```{.bash filename=\"Terminal\"}\nsbatch run_calling.sh\n```\n\n\nTerminal\n\nsbatch run_calling.sh",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#links-between-pages",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#links-between-pages",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Links between pages",
    "text": "Links between pages\nLink to the .qmd file with a relative path. Quarto turns it into the right web address.\nSee [Nextcloud](../computing/nextcloud.qmd).\nJump to a heading: [shared/geno layout](../computing/hpc.qmd#sharedgeno-layout).",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#images",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#images",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Images",
    "text": "Images\n![Seed chipping setup](images/seed-chipping.jpg){fig-alt=\"Razor blade, cutting surface, and labeled 2 mL tubes on a bench\" width=\"70%\"}\nThe text in [ ] is the caption. fig-alt is read by screen readers, so describe what is in the picture.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#diagrams",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#diagrams",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Diagrams",
    "text": "Diagrams\nQuarto draws Mermaid diagrams from plain text.\n```{mermaid}\nflowchart LR\n  A[Harvest] --&gt; B[Weigh] --&gt; C[NIR scan] --&gt; D[Upload]\n```\n\n\n\n\n\n\nflowchart LR\n  A[Harvest] --&gt; B[Weigh] --&gt; C[NIR scan] --&gt; D[Upload]",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
  {
    "objectID": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#running-r-code",
    "href": "contributing/quarto-syntax.html#running-r-code",
    "title": "Quarto syntax",
    "section": "Running R code",
    "text": "Running R code\nA chunk with {r} runs when the page renders and shows its output. Remove engine: markdown from the page header if you add one, and commit _freeze/ afterwards (see Contributing).\n```{r}\n#| label: fig-yield\n#| fig-cap: \"Fruit weight by entry\"\nlibrary(ggplot2)\nggplot(pheno, aes(entry, fruit_wt)) + geom_boxplot()\n```\nTo show R code without running it, leave off the braces: ```r.",
    "crumbs": [
      "Home",
      "Contributing",
      "Quarto syntax"
    ]
  },
